MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

It is not a bug. It is a change of 'labeling'. Instead of 'Robust',
lavaan (0.6-13) now prints 'Scaled'. Because that is a more accurate
description of what is going on: the test statistics (in the first
column) are literally scaled by a certain scaling factor (and sometimes
shifted) to obtain the results in the second column.

The term 'Robust' is rather vague, and may be too optimistic in some
settings. For example, the 'scaled' RMSEA or CFI fit measures turn out
to be not so robust after all. See for example

Savalei, V. (2021) Improving Fit Indices In SEM with categorical data.
Multivariate Behavioral Research, 56(3), 390-407.
https://doi.org/10.1080/00273171.2020.1717922

Yves.

