Hi Keith, see this paper: https://doi.org/10.1080/10705511.2021.1982716 (and in particular, Appendix D). I think it's very new. But the usual approach of labeling the offending parameter and setting an inequality constraint would have also worked in this case; this new syntax was just on my mind because I was recently playing with it in an attempt to rescue some ill-behaved bifactor models.

